<title>FRANCE: CYCLING-PARIS-ROUBAIX CLASSIC STATISTICS.</title>
<headline>CYCLING-PARIS-ROUBAIX CLASSIC STATISTICS.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-04-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Statistical background on the</p>
<p>Paris-Roubaix cycling classic which is being staged on Sunday:</p>
<p>Last 10 winners:</p>
<p> 1987 - Eric Vanderaerden (Belgium)	</p>
<p> 1988 - Dirk Demol (Belgium)		 </p>
<p> 1989 - Jean-Marie Wampers (Belgium)     </p>
<p> 1990 - Eddy Planckaert (Belgium)	  </p>
<p> 1991 - Marc Madiot (France)		</p>
<p> 1992 - Gilbert Duclos-Lassalle (France)</p>
<p> 1993 - Gilbert Duclos-Lassalle (France)</p>
<p> 1994 - Andrei Tchmil (Ukraine)     </p>
<p> 1995 - Franco Ballerini (Italy)    </p>
<p> 1996 - Johan Museeuw (Belgium)	 </p>
<p>Records:</p>
<p>Four victories - Roger de Vlaeminck (Belgium) 1972, 1974,</p>
<p>	  1975, 1977</p>
<p>    3 - Francesco Moser (Italy) 1978, 1979, 1980</p>
<p>	  Eddy Merckx (Belgium) 1968, 1970, 1973</p>
<p>	  Rik Van Looy (Belgium) 1961, 1962, 1965</p>
<p>	  Gaston Rebry (Belgium) 1931, 1934, 1935</p>
<p>	  Octave Lapize (France) 1909, 1910, 1911</p>
<p>    2 - Gilbert Duclos-Lassalle (France) 1992, 1993</p>
<p>	  Marc Madiot (France) 1985, 1991</p>
<p>	  Sean Kelly (Ireland) 1984, 1986</p>
<p>	  Rik Van Steenbergen (Belgium) 1948, 1952</p>
<p>	  Georges Claes (Belgium) 1946, 1947</p>
<p>	  Henri Pelissier (France) 1919, 1921</p>
<p>	  Charles Crupelandt (France) 1912, 1914</p>
<p>	  Hippolyte Aucouturier (France) 1903, 1904</p>
<p>	  Lucien Lesna (France) 1901, 1902</p>
<p>	  Maurice Garin (France) 1897, 1898  </p>
<p>Fastest average speed :  Peter Post 45.129 kph (1964)</p>
